# SQL SELECT Statement — Sorting the Result Set

> Notes from: *DB0101EN – SELECT statement Sorting result sets* (Cognitive Class / Big Data University)

## 1. Result sets are unordered by default

```sql
SELECT * FROM book;
```

- Without any sorting instruction, rows come back in **no guaranteed order** — often just the order they exist in storage
- To control the order, use the **`ORDER BY`** clause

---

## 2. ORDER BY — sort by column name

```sql
SELECT title FROM book
ORDER BY title;
```

- Add `ORDER BY <column>` at the end of the SELECT statement
- Default sort direction is **ascending (A→Z, low→high)**
- Example result — titles sorted alphabetically:

```
TITLE
--------------------------------
Database Fundamentals
Getting started with DB2 App Dev
Getting started with DB2 Express-C
Getting started with WAS CE
```

---

## 3. ORDER BY — sort using column NUMBER instead of name

```sql
SELECT title FROM book
ORDER BY 1;
```

- Instead of typing the column name, you can use its **position number** in the SELECT column list
- `1` refers to the 1st column listed (`title`), `2` would refer to the 2nd column, etc.
- Useful shorthand, but less readable — column names are usually clearer in real code

---

## 4. Sorting by a different column (e.g. PAGES)

```sql
SELECT * FROM book
ORDER BY pages;
```

- Sorts the entire result set based on the values in the `PAGES` column
- Ascending by default → book with fewest pages appears first

---

## 5. Ascending vs Descending

```sql
SELECT * FROM book
ORDER BY pages ASC;   -- ascending (default, can be omitted)

SELECT * FROM book
ORDER BY pages DESC;  -- descending (highest to lowest)
```

- `ASC` = ascending (default if omitted)
- `DESC` = descending — must be stated explicitly

---

## Key Takeaways

| Concept | Syntax | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| Sort ascending (default) | `ORDER BY column` | A→Z / low→high |
| Sort descending | `ORDER BY column DESC` | Z→A / high→low |
| Sort by column position | `ORDER BY 1` | Use column's number in SELECT list instead of its name |
| Sort by any column | `ORDER BY pages`, `ORDER BY title`, etc. | Not limited to columns shown in SELECT |

